1. before performing check in powershell administrator:
minikube version
kubectl version --client
docker --version
2. if minikube and kubectel is not there then paste this:
winget install -e --id Kubernetes.kubectl
kubectl version --client
winget install Kubernetes.minikube
minikube version

then in seperate powershell run this:
1. Start Minikube
Command: minikube start
Expected Output: Done! kubectl is now configured to use "minikube" cluster
2. Verify Cluster
Command: kubectl get nodes
Expected Output: minikube Ready
3. Create Deployment
Command: kubectl create deployment nginx --image=nginx
Expected Output: deployment.apps/nginx created
4. Check Pods
Command: kubectl get pods
Expected Output: nginx-xxxxx Running
5. Expose Service
Command: kubectl expose deployment nginx --type=NodePort --port=80
Expected Output: service/nginx exposed
6. Check Service
Command: kubectl get services
Expected Output: nginx NodePort
7. Open Application
Command: minikube service nginx
Expected Output: Browser opens NGINX page
8. minikube dashboard
This opens the Kubernetes Dashboard in your browser.
Final Result: Browser displays "Welcome to nginx!"
